  (4.92 g/L, Berg & Keefer 1958, Table 1 as reproduced by the AWRI -- the
  primary was not reached), because that is the ceiling of a wine-ED
  concentrate loop: the salt the stack moves is sparingly soluble, and the
  loop is bled to stay under it.  Declared as K+ and HC4H4O6- only (the
  brine's own tartrate speciation is not resolved; announced simplification).
